# Parse-analyzer — dev context

## Stack
- **Next.js 14** (Pages Router). [`pages/index.tsx`](pages/index.tsx) is **Analyze** at `/` with **Solo** | **Compare** subtabs (player-1-only vs side-by-side); [`pages/analyze.tsx`](pages/analyze.tsx) redirects to `/`. [`components/analyze/SoloFightView.tsx`](components/analyze/SoloFightView.tsx) and [`CompareFightView.tsx`](components/analyze/CompareFightView.tsx) hold the two bodies. [`pages/_app.tsx`](pages/_app.tsx) wraps `AppSessionProvider` → `AnalyzePageCacheProvider` → **`FightAnalysisProvider`** (WCL URL, load, dual chat threads, `analysisSubtab`, auth). [`components/AppNav.tsx`](components/AppNav.tsx) holds the global compare URL + auth strip.
- **Claude**: [`lib/wclClient/index.ts`](lib/wclClient/index.ts) `callAI()` POSTs to [`pages/api/ai.ts`](pages/api/ai.ts). Fight text is built by [`lib/buildContext/index.ts`](lib/buildContext/index.ts) `buildRichContext()` (compare) or `buildRichContextPlayerOne()` (analyze tab) and sent as the **system** prompt.

## Critical: client-side context
- `buildRichContext` / `buildRichContextPlayerOne` run in the **browser** (from `FightAnalysisContext`). **Do not** use `fs` or server-only reads for prompt text. Static knowledge must be **imported** from bundled modules (e.g. [`lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts`](lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts), [`lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts`](lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts), [`lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts`](lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts) — JSON snapshots under [`knowledge/wowhead/scraped/`](knowledge/wowhead/scraped/)).

## Knowledge corpora
- **Wowhead summaries**: [`knowledge/guides/`](knowledge/guides/) — **Wowhead-only** authoring policy; see [`knowledge/guides/README.md`](knowledge/guides/README.md). Sync human markdown → [`lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts`](lib/knowledge/embeddedGuides.ts) when editing bodies.
- **SimulationCraft APL**: vendored `.simc` under [`knowledge/simc/`](knowledge/simc/). After changing the file, run **`npm run embed-simc`** to regenerate [`lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts`](lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts). GPL-3.0 upstream; see [`knowledge/simc/README.md`](knowledge/simc/README.md). The SimC block is **opt-in** in the UI (`simcCompareEnabled`) unless the user sends the **SimC + Wowhead** preset, which forces SimC when available for the spec.
- **Wowhead scraped guides**: JSON under [`knowledge/wowhead/scraped/`](knowledge/wowhead/scraped/) via **`npm run scrape-wowhead-frost`**. Bundled for Claude in [`lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts`](lib/knowledge/embeddedWowhead.ts). Opt-in via preset `PRESET_CASTS_VS_SIMC_WOWHEAD` in [`lib/styles.ts`](lib/styles.ts) (forces SimC + Wowhead context for that message). Scraped data currently covers **Frost Mage (specId 64)**; extend imports when adding specs.
- Class reference (Wowhead summary) uses **`talentDiff.specId`** when present. SimC embed matches specs listed in [`embeddedSimc.ts`](lib/knowledge/embeddedSimc.ts).

## Fight pipeline (for context changes)
- WCL fetch/process: [`lib/fightAnalysis/`](lib/fightAnalysis/), game state: [`lib/gameState/`](lib/gameState/). Rich prompt sections use [`lib/buildContext/formatters.ts`](lib/buildContext/formatters.ts).

## SimulationCraft upstream (simulationcraft/simc, branch `midnight`)
Facts from the SimC repo READMEs—use so we don’t misuse vendored APL files:

- **`ActionPriorityLists/`** holds **generated** raw APL text (`.simc`). Upstream says these files **must not be manually edited**; they are produced from **`engine/class_modules/`** and **`engine/class_modules/apl/`** (C++ / converter pipeline).
- **`ActionPriorityLists/default/`** — default lists per spec/module from that generation path.
- **`ActionPriorityLists/assisted_combat/`** — lists derived from Blizzard **DBC** tables (`AssistedCombat`, `AssistedCombatStep`, `AssistedCombatRule`), not the same as `default/`.
- **APL snippet shape** (for reading/parsing): lines like `actions=…`, `actions+=/spell,if=condition`, named lists `actions.list+=/…`, comments `# …`. Not a full SimC **profile** (gear/talents/options)—those are separate.
- **This app**: we **vendor snapshots** (e.g. `knowledge/simc/mage_frost.midnight.simc`) for Claude context. Refresh by re-downloading **raw** `midnight` URLs and `npm run embed-simc`—do not treat our copy as the place to “fix” SimC’s canonical APL (real fixes belong upstream in SimC).
- **Docs / community**: SimC wiki (starters guide, common issues), Discord **SimCMinMax** — for semantics disputes, not for embedding whole dumps into parse-ai.

## Conventions
- Prefer **small, focused diffs**; match existing patterns in touched files.
- Run **`npm run build`** (and tests if touching logic) before finishing.
